From 83e19c483df65e0f5c81afef7f1d6674c207541a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:11:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add gfx11 CK Tile Quant2 MoE

Add native wave32 INT8 MoE execution for gfx1100.

Reason:
- Legacy CK Quant2 assumes wave64 and is unsafe.
- The Triton fallback is correct but slower.

Fix:
- Require the exact gfx11 Quant2 kernel names.
- Require runtime architecture gfx1100.
- Preserve existing dispatch for every other call.
- Add CK Tile WMMA stage-one and stage-two kernels.
- Decode padded token and top-k route identifiers.
- Gate dispatch with a validated problem descriptor.
- Restrict CK to validated input and scale contracts.
- Add validated tail-K and model-sized problems.
- Keep unsupported gfx11 cases on Triton.
- Skip unusable FP4 generator entries off gfx950.

Testing
- Built gfx90a, gfx1100, and gfx1151 targets.
- Passed 21 gfx11 tests, including Mori scatter.
- Checked partial M, tail K, last expert, and guards.
- Repeated CK runs produced identical output.
- Validated the 4096x14336 model-sized problem.
- CK measured 2140 us versus Triton at 2381 us.
- Compared CK output with Triton and Torch.

Tools used:
- GPT-5.6 Sol: coding agent

Signed-off-by: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
